{"commit": "bd3770c5852d7e01fa74635c52100f0e4f4c34f4", "id": "bd3770c5852d7e01fa74635c52100f0e4f4c34f4-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Reversal changes are not part of the upstream fix", "repo": "https://github.com/unicode-rs/unicode-normalization", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T003047Z-90c96695", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/bd3770c5852d7e01fa74635c52100f0e4f4c34f4-1/20260924T003047Z-90c96695/origin.json": "a2a93fb8500b111ebad99a3dc398889d7b7c9ba82f85c471ae8aeed28ec74515", "evidence/bd3770c5852d7e01fa74635c52100f0e4f4c34f4-1/20260924T003047Z-90c96695/proposal.json": "2f720ee8c52740479dd9d1d41584ff713f89da55b15bc2d3078234d835a373ea"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "unicode-normalization", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix corner case in Hangul composition", "summary": "`char::compose` did not guard against the T-base sentinel codepoint `U+11A7` \u2014 the slot between T-jamos, not an actual trailing consonant. Composing any LV syllable with `U+11A7` incorrectly produced an LVT syllable. The fix rejects the T-base sentinel and requires the T-jamo to be strictly `> T_BASE`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:30:47.387264+00:00"}
{"commit": "e4fd0e1b21f39e7d8ff35da53eb11d0624bbf6cc", "id": "e4fd0e1b21f39e7d8ff35da53eb11d0624bbf6cc-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/unicode-rs/unicode-normalization", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T003058Z-550cfd13", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/e4fd0e1b21f39e7d8ff35da53eb11d0624bbf6cc-1/20260924T003058Z-550cfd13/origin.json": "ed36b97978cc4c05b99697f0783f41541b73acc3875d7691e2c2f96fb94e61cf", "evidence/e4fd0e1b21f39e7d8ff35da53eb11d0624bbf6cc-1/20260924T003058Z-550cfd13/proposal.json": "5477b9977c1cb31eef80005151f9cf9ca1aec5113b851adbb74a48e4cb9c8e86"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "unicode-normalization", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Do not further compose LVT hangul precomposed syllable blocks", "summary": "`char::compose` had a match arm that accepted any `S_BASE..=S_LAST` LV or LVT syllable and unconditionally offset into another LVT cell. For LVT syllables (which already carry a trailing consonant), composing with another T-jamo silently produced a different LVT syllable instead of `None`. The fix restricts the arm to actual LV syllables.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:30:58.817004+00:00"}
